{"uid":"ece8d20b9d472ff7","name":"test_validate_date_modified_and_date_modified_gmt","fullName":"tests.customers.api.test_update_customer#test_validate_date_modified_and_date_modified_gmt","historyId":"44d0a71eb1b8f8c32eb1adb4f82c3d75","time":{"start":1790235159064,"stop":1790235159526,"duration":462},"description":"\nVerify that customer modification timestamps are consistent between API and database.\n\nThis test validates the following:\n\n1. Updating a customer changes the modification timestamp.\n2. The API `date_modified` field matches the database `last_update` timestamp\n   within expected system behavior.\n3. The original `date_created` value remains unchanged after update.\n\nImportant notes about timestamps:\n\n• WordPress stores timestamps in site-local time (no timezone info).\n• WooCommerce REST API returns timestamps in UTC.\n• Due to DST (Daylight Saving Time), DB and API may differ by ±1 hour.\n\n\uD83D\uDC49 Therefore:\n   We do NOT assert exact equality.\n   We assert that timestamps are aligned within known system offsets.\n\nAccepted differences:\n    - 0 seconds   → perfect match\n    - 3600 seconds → DST / timezone shift\n\nTest flow:\n    1. Fetch a random active customer from DB\n    2. Capture DB timestamps before update\n    3. Update the customer via API\n    4. Validate identity and business changes\n    5. Validate timestamp consistency between API and DB\n\nTest strongly proves:\n   - Customer was updated\n   - API returned updated timestamps\n   - DB persisted timestamps correctly\n   - Timestamps are monotonic\n   - Timezone/DST behavior is correct\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>Verify that customer modification timestamps are consistent between API and database.</p>\n<p>This test validates the following:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Updating a customer changes the modification timestamp.</li>\n<li>The API <code>date_modified</code> field matches the database <code>last_update</code> timestamp<br />\nwithin expected system behavior.</li>\n<li>The original <code>date_created</code> value remains unchanged after update.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Important notes about timestamps:</p>\n<p>• WordPress stores timestamps in site-local time (no timezone info).<br />\n• WooCommerce REST API returns timestamps in UTC.<br />\n• Due to DST (Daylight Saving Time), DB and API may differ by ±1 hour.</p>\n<p>\uD83D\uDC49 Therefore:<br />\nWe do NOT assert exact equality.<br />\nWe assert that timestamps are aligned within known system offsets.</p>\n<p>Accepted differences:<br />\n- 0 seconds   → perfect match<br />\n- 3600 seconds → DST / timezone shift</p>\n<p>Test flow:<br />\n1. Fetch a random active customer from DB<br />\n2. Capture DB timestamps before update<br />\n3. Update the customer via API<br />\n4. Validate identity and business changes<br />\n5. Validate timestamp consistency between API and DB</p>\n<p>Test strongly proves:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer was updated</li>\n<li>API returned updated timestamps</li>\n<li>DB persisted timestamps correctly</li>\n<li>Timestamps are monotonic</li>\n<li>Timezone/DST behavior is correct</li>\n</ul>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1790235142760,"stop":1790235142760,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_session_faker","time":{"start":1790235142760,"stop":1790235142761,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1790235142760,"stop":1790235142760,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_verify_url","time":{"start":1790235142760,"stop":1790235142760,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"base_url","time":{"start":1790235142760,"stop":1790235142760,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"api_base_url","time":{"start":1790235142761,"stop":1790235142762,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"api_client","time":{"start":1790235142762,"stop":1790235143488,"duration":726},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"shared_api_resources","time":{"start":1790235157742,"stop":1790235157747,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"all_resources","time":{"start":1790235157747,"stop":1790235157747,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"customers_dao","time":{"start":1790235159063,"stop":1790235159064,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"customer_helper","time":{"start":1790235159063,"stop":1790235159063,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"create_valid_customer","time":{"start":1790235159064,"stop":1790235159064,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false}],"testStage":{"description":"\nVerify that customer modification timestamps are consistent between API and database.\n\nThis test validates the following:\n\n1. Updating a customer changes the modification timestamp.\n2. The API `date_modified` field matches the database `last_update` timestamp\n   within expected system behavior.\n3. The original `date_created` value remains unchanged after update.\n\nImportant notes about timestamps:\n\n• WordPress stores timestamps in site-local time (no timezone info).\n• WooCommerce REST API returns timestamps in UTC.\n• Due to DST (Daylight Saving Time), DB and API may differ by ±1 hour.\n\n\uD83D\uDC49 Therefore:\n   We do NOT assert exact equality.\n   We assert that timestamps are aligned within known system offsets.\n\nAccepted differences:\n    - 0 seconds   → perfect match\n    - 3600 seconds → DST / timezone shift\n\nTest flow:\n    1. Fetch a random active customer from DB\n    2. Capture DB timestamps before update\n    3. Update the customer via API\n    4. Validate identity and business changes\n    5. Validate timestamp consistency between API and DB\n\nTest strongly proves:\n   - Customer was updated\n   - API returned updated timestamps\n   - DB persisted timestamps correctly\n   - Timestamps are monotonic\n   - Timezone/DST behavior is correct\n","status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[{"uid":"abdf1e128baf2414","name":"log","source":"abdf1e128baf2414.txt","type":"text/plain","size":8384}],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":1,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"hasContent":true,"attachmentStep":false},"afterStages":[{"name":"customers_dao::<lambda